'''Yuru''' (Juru) is an extinct [[Australian Aboriginal languages|Australian Aboriginal language]] formerly spoken at the mouth of the [[Burdekin River]] in the state of [[Queensland]]. A single vocabulary collected by John O'Connor and published in ''[[The Australian Race]]'' by [[Edward Curr]]<ref>{{Citation |last=O'Connor |first=John |title=Mouths of the Burdekin River |date=1886 |work=The Australian Race |volume=II |pages=454–455 |url=https://archive.org/details/cu31924026093827/page/n7/mode/2up |access-date=2026-03-11 |place=Melbourne |publisher=John Ferres, Government Printer}}</ref> is the only source on the language.<ref>{{Cite book |last=Terrill |first=Angela |title=Biri |date=1998 |publisher=LINCOM Europa |isbn=978-3-89586-532-9 |series=Languages of the world Materials |location=München Newcastle}}</ref>{{Reference page|page=86}}<ref>{{Cite journal |last=Breen |first=Gavan |date=January 2009 |title=The Biri Dialects and their Neighbours |url=https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/03721426.2009.10887121 |journal=Transactions of the Royal Society of South Australia |language=en |volume=133 |issue=2 |pages=219–256 |doi=10.1080/03721426.2009.10887121 |issn=0372-1426|url-access=subscription }}</ref>

== Classification ==
Yuru has been classified as [[Nyawaygic languages|Nyawaygic]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=Glottolog 5.3 - Yuru |url=https://glottolog.org/resource/languoid/id/yuru1264 |access-date=2026-03-11 |website=glottolog.org}}</ref>

